gram targeted towards the unemployed  the idea of extending european exchange  to a different level besides university  education is not new and it seems like  the tide is turning  the netherlands education levels are  split between mbo hbo and wo mboers  usually pursue vocational education and  are more euroskeptic and wors usually  pursue university and are less  naturally w owers were the ones who  usually did the erasmus exchange but the  amount of mbao students abroad with help  from eu grants has also been increasing  this increased movement has been  encouraged and alexander pechthold the  former dutch leader of de sas incesto  has said that mbo students should have  better access to european exchange  programs europe is no game for the happy  few it needs to show that it's  absolutely necessary for all of us  you can also see other examples like  volt netherlands explicitly pushing to  broaden erasmus plus for mbo and hbo  students as one of their policy  standpoints in the last dutch election  evaluations have shown that the early  erasmus plus program was able to  facilitate a european identity among a  sample of vocational students with 66  feeling more european after and over 72  percent declaring to have a larger  interest in the eu  with the set goal of reaching 10 million  more students erasmus plus over the  course of 2021 and 2027 is set to focus  more on inclusion and the new program is  doubling the funding for vocational  education from 2.9 million to up to 4.4  whether this new more inclusive erasmus  budget plus the additional alma program  announced this year will actually  produce a larger european identity among  europeans who feel that connection the  least  is honestly difficult to determine  but whether this is part of the european  union's goal of producing a stronger  european identity  that's undeniable  our ultimate goal  should be that erasmus  is not become  an option but a fundamental right for  all europeans this new reinforced ro